 Detection Rule: Lateral Movement via Administrative Shares & Net Use

 Overview
Detects potential lateral movement by internal workstations or compromised standard accounts attempting to map administrative shares (`C$`, `ADMIN$`, `IPC$`) on critical servers or domain controllers using the `net use` command-line utility (Event ID 4688).

MITRE ATT&CK Mapping
- **Tactic:** Lateral Movement (TA0008)
- **Technique:** Remote Services: SMB/Windows Admin Shares (T1021.002)

 Splunk SPL Detection Query
spl
index=windows EventCode=4688 
(Process_Command_Line="*net use*" AND (Process_Command_Line="*\\C$*" OR Process_Command_Line="*\\ADMIN$*" OR Process_Command_Line="*\\IPC$*"))
| table _time, host, Account_Name, ParentProcessName, Process_Command_Line
